/*--------------------------------*- C++ -*----------------------------------*\
  VMFLGPU003 -- laminar flow in a lid-driven TRIANGULAR CAVITY (Ansys Fluid
  Dynamics Verification Manual, Release 2026 R1, p. 229), with EVERY linear
  solve routed through petsc4Foam.

  __MATTYPE__ / __VECTYPE__ are substituted by run_vmflgpu003.sh, exactly as
  VMFLGPU001 and VMFLGPU002 do:

      GPU arm            : aijcusparse / cuda
      forced-CPU control : aij        / standard

  BOTH ARMS ARE OTHERWISE BYTE-IDENTICAL.  That identity is the entire basis on
  which limb B is a statement about WHERE the linear algebra ran and about
  nothing else: same mesh, same schemes, same relaxation, same outer loop, same
  tolerances, same outer iteration count.

  THE OUTER NUMERICS ARE THE CPU PARENT'S, CHARACTER FOR CHARACTER.  VMFL011's
  frozen system/fvSolution carries `consistent yes`, THREE non-orthogonal
  correctors, pRefCell 0 / pRefValue 0 and relaxation 0.7 / 0.7, and those are
  the numerics under which the parent's MEASURED convergence points were
  obtained (VMFL011-R2 log.simpleFoam: the initial residuals of Ux, Uy and p all
  fall below 1e-7 and STAY below it from iteration 259 / 488 / 1455 at
  L1 / L2 / L3).  Those measurements are this case's endTime basis and its cost
  basis, so changing the outer loop would silently invalidate both.  ONLY the
  linear solvers change -- and the linear solver IS the object under
  verification.

  Three non-orthogonal correctors are NOT a free parameter here: the mesh is a
  DEGENERATE-HEX prism mesh collapsed onto the cavity apex, so cell
  non-orthogonality is real and the parent's corrector count is what its
  convergence record was measured under.

  What changed, and why:
    p : PCG/DIC        -> petsc, ksp_type cg    + pc_type jacobi  (symmetric)
    U : PBiCGStab/DILU -> petsc, ksp_type bcgs  + pc_type jacobi  (asymmetric)
  The OUTER tolerances (1e-12) and relTol (p 0.01, U 0.1) are the parent's own
  values, unchanged; limb B's 1e-4 bound is derived from them in
  PREREGISTRATION.md section 6.2.

  NO residualControl: every level runs to EXACTLY endTime so that CLAUDE.md
  rule 4's "last time == endTime" and the `Time =` line-count clause are
  literally testable, and so that BOTH ARMS TAKE THE SAME NUMBER OF OUTER
  ITERATIONS.  Iterative convergence is judged AFTER the run, by the comparator,
  from the residual history and from the GATE QUANTITY'S OWN plateau.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
FoamFile
{
    version     2.0;
    format      ascii;
    class       dictionary;
    object      fvSolution;
}
// * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * //

solvers
{
    p
    {
        solver          petsc;
        petsc
        {
            options
            {
                ksp_type        cg;
                pc_type         jacobi;
                mat_type        __MATTYPE__;
                vec_type        __VECTYPE__;
            }
            caching { matrix { update always; } preconditioner { update always; } }
        }
        tolerance       1e-12;
        relTol          0.01;
    }

    U
    {
        solver          petsc;
        petsc
        {
            options
            {
                ksp_type        bcgs;
                pc_type         jacobi;
                mat_type        __MATTYPE__;
                vec_type        __VECTYPE__;
            }
            caching { matrix { update always; } preconditioner { update always; } }
        }
        tolerance       1e-12;
        relTol          0.1;
    }
}

SIMPLE
{
    nNonOrthogonalCorrectors 3;
    consistent      yes;
    pRefCell        0;
    pRefValue       0;
}

relaxationFactors
{
    equations
    {
        U               0.7;
        p               0.7;
    }
}

// ************************************************************************* //
